node_modules/
*.tgz
/tmp/
audits/
# Page snapshots. Generated by the engine and by the e2e tests, always relative to the
# CURRENT DIRECTORY — so a test run from the repository root leaves one here. Ignored rather
# than tolerated: a stray capture in this tree changes the repo's own language signal, and the
# failures then land somewhere else entirely (`resolveLang`, in files that never touched it).
#
# The CONTENTS are ignored, not the directory: git will not re-include a path whose parent is
# excluded, so `.ultra11y/` followed by a negation silently does nothing. `.ultra11y/*` leaves
# the directory itself visible, which is what makes the exception below take effect.
.ultra11y/*
# …EXCEPT the verdict ledger, which is the opposite kind of file. A snapshot is a build
# artefact of a run; a ledger is a CLAIM ABOUT THIS CODEBASE — one entry per adjudicated
# criterion, with its justification, its citations and a fingerprint of the evidence it was
# ruled against. It belongs in review next to the code it describes, and committing it is what
# lets a keyless CI job replay the grid and gate on it with no model in the loop.
#
# It holds justifications and citation snippets, not serialized pages, and it sits under a path
# no capture is written to — so it does not move the repo's language signal the way a stray
# .ultra11y/pages/ does, which is the only reason the blanket ignore above exists.
!.ultra11y/verdicts/
coverage/
.DS_Store
# Claude Code session dir — the harness locks .claude/workflows/ against external
# reads/writes, so git must not descend into it. The canonical verification workflow
# is versioned at .superpowers/verification/verify-impl.workflow.js instead.
.claude/
# verify worklist output (root only; anchored so it can't shadow
# skills/.../references/verify.md on case-insensitive filesystems)
/VERIFY.todo.json
/VERIFY.md

# adjudication worklist output — the twin of VERIFY.* above, and anchored for the same
# reason. `verify --manual --out .` writes these at whatever directory it was run from, so a
# run against this repository's own sources leaves them here. They were tracked once
# (ADJUDICATE.md, ADJUDICATE.todo.json, ADJUDICATE.verdicts.json, adjudicate/1.1.1.md,
# adjudicate/1.2.1.md, from a 2026-08-11 run over 2 criteria); nothing read them — the Action
# writes and reads audits/ADJUDICATE.*, a different path entirely.
/ADJUDICATE.md
/ADJUDICATE.todo.json
/ADJUDICATE.verdicts.json
/adjudicate/
